From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable update checks and `openchamber update`: the image is read-only

On Cherry, OpenChamber is part of a read-only system image, and a new
version only comes with a new image. So there is nothing to check for:

- checkForUpdates reports no update without asking the update API, nor
  the npm registry and GitHub it falls back to. That covers the web UI's
  update-check route (no banner, and the install route answers "No update
  available").
- `openchamber update` fails with a message that updates are disabled on
  this platform, through the CLI's usual error path, in JSON mode too.

Upstream: not applicable, Cherry-specific
Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff -ru a/node_modules/@openchamber/web/bin/lib/commands-update.js b/node_modules/@openchamber/web/bin/lib/commands-update.js
--- a/node_modules/@openchamber/web/bin/lib/commands-update.js
+++ b/node_modules/@openchamber/web/bin/lib/commands-update.js
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 
 function createUpdateCommand({ importFromFilePath, packageManagerPath, serveCommand }) {
   return async function updateCommand(options = {}) {
+    throw new Error('Updates are disabled on this platform: OpenChamber is part of the system image, and a new version comes with a new image.');
     const showOutput = shouldRenderHumanOutput(options);
     const updateSpin = createSpinner(options);
 
diff -ru a/node_modules/@openchamber/web/server/lib/package-manager.js b/node_modules/@openchamber/web/server/lib/package-manager.js
--- a/node_modules/@openchamber/web/server/lib/package-manager.js
+++ b/node_modules/@openchamber/web/server/lib/package-manager.js
@@ -792,6 +792,7 @@
 
 export async function checkForUpdates(options = {}) {
   const currentVersion = options.currentVersion || getCurrentVersion();
+  return { available: false, currentVersion };
   const pm = detectPackageManager();
   const appType = normalizeAppType(options.appType);
   const platform = normalizePlatform(options.platform);
